---
import BaseLayout from "../components/BaseLayout.astro";
import PageHeader from "../components/PageHeader.astro";
import PlaceholderBox from "../components/PlaceholderBox.astro";
import { SITE, href } from "../site.config";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Partnership"
  description="SAWiE Ecosystem, the industrial partner, and Namal University."
>
  <PageHeader
    title="Partnership"
    intro="An industry partnership and a university project. What each side did, and what public sources confirm."
  />
  <div class="container">
    <h2>SAWiE Ecosystem — industrial partner</h2>
    <p>
      The project report names SAWiE Ecosystem as the project's primary industrial partner
      (§1.8). The collaboration included mentorship, technical guidance, and industry insight; an
      executive visit to Namal University; and regular video calls.
    </p>
    <p>
      Description, paraphrased from public sources: SAWiE
      (Sustainable Agriculture, Water &amp; Intelligent Ecosystem) offers data-driven farm advisory
      services using satellite and sensor data, machine learning, and mapping, aimed mainly at
      smallholder farmers. Its own site describes work with farmers in Pakistan. Use of the name,
      this description, and the website link is confirmed by the project lead, 12 Nov 2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      Official website: <a href={SITE.links.sawieWebsite} rel="noopener">sawie.net</a> ·
      About page: <a href={SITE.links.sawieAbout} rel="noopener">sawie.net/about</a>
    </p>
    <PlaceholderBox text="logo permission (not approved) — no logo, photo, or quote is shown" />

    <h2>Fritz Böhmler</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Fritz Böhmler — {SITE.person.boehmlerTitle}, SAWiE.</strong> The project report
      calls him CEO (§1.8). SAWiE's announcement of 30 April 2025 of his appointment as Chief Executive Officer
      also signs him as Managing Director, and Namal University's newsletter uses the combined
      title "CEO and Managing Director of SAWiE, Germany". This page uses the combined title and
      shows both sources. Inclusion and role wording are confirmed by the project lead,
      12 Nov 2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      Mr Böhmler is also listed as co-supervisor (industry partner) on the
      <a href={href("/team")}>Team</a> page, per the project lead's decision of 12 November 2026.
    </p>
    <p>
      SAWiE announcement (link only):
      <a href={SITE.links.sawieCeoAnnouncement} rel="noopener">SAWiE welcomes Mr Fritz Böhmler as new CEO</a>
    </p>
    <div class="notice">
      <p>
        <strong>On "Germany".</strong> Public sources link Mr Böhmler personally with Germany, and
        Namal University's newsletter labels the engagement "SAWiE, Germany". SAWiE's own site
        describes Pakistan-based operations, and no Germany office was found on its site. This page
        therefore does not call SAWiE a German company. It states the Germany link only as sourced
        above.
      </p>
    </div>
    <p>No photo, logo, or quote from Mr Böhmler is shown. No quote from him exists in the project report.</p>

    <h2>Namal University</h2>
    <p>
      The project was completed at the Department of Computer Science, Namal University,
      30-KM Talagang Road, Mianwali, Pakistan (report title page). The university's Office of
      Research, Innovation, and Commercialization (ORIC) organised AgriFusion 2025. Use of the
      university name on this public site is confirmed by the project lead, 12 Nov 2026. Logo use
      is not approved.
    </p>
    <p>
      University website:
      <a href={SITE.links.namalUniversity} rel="noopener">namal.edu.pk</a>
    </p>
    <PlaceholderBox text="logo permission (not approved), and ownership/licensing decision for code, models, and data" />

    <h2>What the partnership did — and did not do</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Did: mentorship, technical guidance, industry insight, a visit, and video collaboration (report §1.8).</li>
      <li>Did not, on the evidence in the report: supply a published expert statement about this project or endorse any result figure. No such statement is quoted here.</li>
      <li>General mentor feedback in the report (Chapter 10) is unattributed and undated. It is not turned into testimonials or quotes anywhere on this site.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      <a href={href("/team")}>Team and supervisors</a> ·
      <a href={href("/field-work")}>Field work</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
